Usual package boilerplate 

```julia 
using Pkg
pkg"activate .; instantiate; precompile"
using CSV, Plots, JSON, BenchmarkTools, Parameters, PerlaTonettiWaugh, DataFrames
gr(fmt = :png)
```

We can instantiate our parameters and settings 

```julia 
parameters = parameter_defaults();
settings = settings_defaults();
```

We can inspect the experiment 

```julia 
@show parameters.d_0, parameters.d_T; 
```

And

```julia 
histogram(settings.tstops)
```

As we can see, the `tstops` are front-loaded. 

Let's run the experiment. 

```julia 
sol = @time solve_transition_FP(parameters, settings);
solved = sol.dynamics_output.results;
```

## Plots 

```julia 
plot(solved.g, legend = false, title = "g")
```

```julia 
plot(solved.Ω, legend = false, title = "Omega")
```

```julia 
plot(solved.z_hat, legend = false, title = "z_hat")
```

```julia 
plot(solved.L_tilde, legend = false, title = "L_tilde")
```
